WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.250 --> 00:00:03.277
Your health data is scattered: DNA, blood

2
00:00:03.277 --> 00:00:06.452
work, a wearable, even the air you breathe.

3
00:00:06.452 --> 00:00:09.701
VitaCrypt joins it into one profile, and its

4
00:00:09.701 --> 00:00:13.023
Lab Agent follows up on every new blood test.

5
00:00:13.023 --> 00:00:18.782
This is our early-stage MVP, live, with synthetic data for a fictional person,

6
00:00:18.782 --> 00:00:19.151
Alex.

7
00:00:19.851 --> 00:00:21.696
The demo needs no sign-up.

8
00:00:21.696 --> 00:00:25.953
Every visitor gets a private copy, deleted after seven days.

9
00:00:26.653 --> 00:00:32.049
Alex connects six sources: two earlier blood tests, seventeen DNA variants,

10
00:00:32.049 --> 00:00:37.661
sleep, steps and heart rate, eight questionnaires, a gut report, and local air

11
00:00:37.661 --> 00:00:38.237
quality.

12
00:00:38.937 --> 00:00:43.296
For this video, Alex is in New Delhi, with real archived air data

13
00:00:43.296 --> 00:00:47.790
from the city: air quality index one hundred ninety one, unhealthy.

14
00:00:48.490 --> 00:00:53.072
Today connects what no single app sees: months of heavy pollution,

15
00:00:53.072 --> 00:00:57.515
a rising inflammation marker, and gene variants studied with it.

16
00:00:57.515 --> 00:01:00.153
Each link is checked against research.

17
00:01:00.153 --> 00:01:05.082
No study tested this combination, so it is labelled a hypothesis, not a

18
00:01:05.082 --> 00:01:05.429
fact.

19
00:01:06.129 --> 00:01:08.317
Then a new blood test arrives.

20
00:01:08.317 --> 00:01:13.862
First, the agent shows its seven fixed steps and what leaves VitaCrypt: gene

21
00:01:13.862 --> 00:01:19.698
and marker names, coded facts for the AI model, never Alex's name, file or exact

22
00:01:19.698 --> 00:01:20.209
values.

23
00:01:20.909 --> 00:01:25.573
It compares the lab with earlier ones, links changes to Alex's

24
00:01:25.573 --> 00:01:30.163
DNA, and searches PubMed and Europe PMC, showing every query.

25
00:01:30.163 --> 00:01:35.956
A language model checks each paper against each claim; fixed rules decide the

26
00:01:35.956 --> 00:01:36.333
plan.

27
00:01:37.033 --> 00:01:39.438
The plan already checks the last one.

28
00:01:39.438 --> 00:01:44.312
Alex did the daylight habit on twenty two of twenty eight days, yet vitamin

29
00:01:44.312 --> 00:01:49.187
D fell, so the agent swaps the habit and adds a question for the clinician.

30
00:01:49.187 --> 00:01:53.737
Supplements appear only as official reference values, never as a dose.

31
00:01:54.437 --> 00:01:59.251
Then it acts, only on Alex's tap: a retest reminder, labs nearby, a

32
00:01:59.251 --> 00:02:04.280
repeat order, and a clinician link with a preview of exactly what they

33
00:02:04.280 --> 00:02:04.567
see.

34
00:02:04.567 --> 00:02:08.160
Orders and lab listings are simulated in the demo.

35
00:02:08.160 --> 00:02:09.669
Every send is logged.

36
00:02:10.369 --> 00:02:13.898
Eight weeks later, with a simulated habit log, the

37
00:02:13.898 --> 00:02:17.498
next lab arrives and the agent grades its own plan.

38
00:02:17.498 --> 00:02:20.251
Vitamin D is improving: keep the habit.

39
00:02:20.251 --> 00:02:25.263
Homocysteine rose despite the habit: try another and ask the clinician.

40
00:02:25.263 --> 00:02:28.651
The LDL habit was rarely done: do it more often.

41
00:02:29.351 --> 00:02:34.025
Once a month, it becomes a one-page report: what changed, what worked,

42
00:02:34.025 --> 00:02:38.631
and what comes next, ready to save as a PDF for the next appointment.

43
00:02:39.331 --> 00:02:43.811
Many sources, one profile, research-checked insights, and an

44
00:02:43.811 --> 00:02:48.142
agent that acts with your permission and learns from every

45
00:02:48.142 --> 00:02:48.441
lab.

46
00:02:48.441 --> 00:02:50.905
Not medical advice, never a dose.

47
00:02:50.905 --> 00:02:54.862
Try the live demo at vitacrypt.xyz/agent.
